m  huge words considering the weight that  that name carries in the series back to  king and he is not fighting fair in a  swordsman sense but apparently all is  fair in love and war so you can't really  blame him his sword also has special  properties and he is able to use the  jagged edges of it in order to trap two  of zoro's swords and take them away he  then delivers a spiked knuckle sandwich  but zoro manages to block it in pretty  epic fashion with his mouth sword soros  seems to look down on this style of  fighting but king has a point when he  says he never understood why people  stick to traditional forms and  techniques in real battle and zorro  being the boss he is doesn't freak out  but just says yeah you're right you  never claim to be a swordsman as he  grabs his three blades again and  although zoro is more geared towards  that traditional school of swordsmanship  he gets what king is saying and says  that even he zorro may bite through  king's throat because he can't afford to  lose here i love it i love the  commitment i love the fact that he's  willing to do whatever it takes this is  such a great matchup and zorro is  finally gonna be pushed hard so  hopefully we see everything he has to  offer and more post time skip hoping to  see that closed eye activate soon still  expecting something to happen from that  then it's pointed out by hyogoro that  zoro looks exactly like the former  daimyo of ringo when he was young  shimotsuki ushimaru their two p's in a  pod and yes they just said the title in  the chapter the similarity really is  uncanny and it makes sense oda did say  zoro would be from japan in the real  world and juan was definitely the japan  of the one piece world apparently  ushimaru was the direct descendant of  the god of the blade shimotsuki ryuma  and since zoro returned shusui to wano  kawamatsu is convinced it's fate so not  only does luffy have chosen one vibes  zorro definitely does as well he may  well be the direct descendant 